      "artist": "Sami Belsous",
      "description": "An architectural masterpiece dating back to the 5th century, the Temple of Zeus with its massive columns reflects the beauty of Greek civilization.\nThe Temple of Zeus in Cyrene, Libya, or \"Temple of Zeus in Shahat,\" is the largest Greek temple in Libya, dedicated to Zeus, the king of the Greek gods. The temple was built in the 5th century BC, featuring massive columns in the classical Doric style. It was destroyed following the Jewish revolt in the city between 116 and 117 AD and was later rebuilt by Emperor Commodus. The temple spans an area of 70 by 32 meters and is supported by two rows of classical Doric columns.",
